ShortDescription: Push and merge pull requests across a network air gap
Description: Git Airlock keeps an isolated machine working against a private Git remote it cannot reach. Commits go to a LAN mirror, a worker on the VPN-connected workstation syncs and merges pull requests, and the isolated machine never touches the private network. Includes a CLI, a multi-repository dashboard, automatic PRs and an MCP server.
